    "vintage natural history plate of the Nile perch Lates niloticus (尼罗尖吻鲈) in side profile: ONE huge imposing predator fish, its body an elongate silver-grey blade washed with electric blue on the back and mother-of-pearl on the flank, the big eye ringed with gold and the jaws tipped with a golden sheen as if wearing gilt spectacles, the wide mouth reaching back past the eye and lined with a fine velvet carpet of needle teeth, the dorsal fin split in two by a deep notch — a strong spiny crescent before a soft lobe — a broad fan-shaped tail, the flank faintly crossed by a few dusky young bars faded to smoke, absolutely NO scattered spots NO black blotch NOT a marlin with a bill, copperplate engraving with watercolor tinting on aged parchment, no text no letters no labels",
